    <briefdescription>
<para>SLO-based adaptive retry configuration (Phase 5, v1.9.0). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>When set together with <computeroutput>sla_deadline</computeroutput>, the scheduler adapts retry behaviour to avoid spending the full SLA budget on retries and prevent cascading SLO violations.</para>
<para>Adaptive rules applied before each retry delay:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>If elapsed task time + computed retry delay &gt; sla_deadline * slo_budget_fraction, the retry delay is clamped to the remaining SLA budget fraction (minimum 0 ms — i.e. retry immediately).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>If the remaining SLA budget (sla_deadline − elapsed) ≤ 0, all further retries are skipped immediately — the task has already exceeded its SLO.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>When the rolling SLO compliance rate (over the last <computeroutput>slo_history_window</computeroutput> executions) drops below <computeroutput>slo_compliance_threshold</computeroutput>, the effective max_retries is clamped to <computeroutput>min_retries_under_pressure</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para>Requires <computeroutput>sla_deadline</computeroutput> to be set; ignored (no-op) otherwise. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
